            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for to steal, then the Telugu for to run away."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ఒకప్పుడు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఒకప్పుడు — okappuḍu — \"at one time; once\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఒకప్పుడు ఇక్కడ ఒక పెద్ద అడవి ఉండేది. okappuḍu ikkaḍa oka pedda aḍavi uṇḍēdi. At one time there was a big forest here."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Stories often open with ఒకప్పుడు (okappuḍu), the way English opens with once upon a time: ఒక, one, and అప్పుడు, then."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఒకప్పుడు (okappuḍu) is a native Telugu compound: oka, \"one\" (DEDR 990), and appuḍu, \"at that time\" (DEDR 4559)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
