          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "రాజు — rāju — \"a king\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆ రాజు చాలా మంచివాడు. ā rāju cālā mañcivāḍu. That king is a very good man."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: రాజులు, rājulu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The capital, రాజధాని, is the seat of the king: the same Sanskrit word sits inside it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "రాజు (rāju) is borrowed from Sanskrit rājan, \"a chieftain, a king\" (CDIAL 10679). Telugu gives it the native ending -ఉ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
